# 5 Carat Radiant Cut Diamond Ring: The $119K vs $28K Truth

A 5 carat radiant cut diamond ring crosses into a different tier. The face-up size is approximately 11.0×8.5mm for an elongated stone — the weight where [The 11mm Statement](#the-11mm-statement) lands, and a radiant cut stops needing introduction.

In current certified market inventory, lab 5ct radiant rings start at [$28,302](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Natural 5ct radiant rings start at [$118,946](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

That gap is 4.2×. At 4ct, the same gap was 10.2×. [The Compression Point](#the-compression-point) explains why the spread narrows here — and what that means for your decision.

**TL;DR:**
- → **The 4.2× Gap:** lab 5ct ring at [$28,302](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), natural entry at [$118,946](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — the gap narrows sharply from the 10.2× at 4ct
- → **Best lab pick:** [5.00ct D-IF IGI $27,442](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Ten Prong WG $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **[$28,302](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — D-IF IGI, 11mm face-up
- → **Natural entry:** [5.01ct G-VS1 GIA $118,086](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Ten Prong WG $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **[$118,946](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — GIA certified, G-VS1
- → **Natural sweet spot:** [5.02ct F-VS1 GIA $147,273](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557946?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [$860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **[$148,133](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557946?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — F-VS1, GIA certified
- → 5ct radiant face-up: ~11.0×8.5mm. Crosses [The 11mm Statement](#the-11mm-statement) — unmistakable from across a room
- → Upgrade from 4ct costs [$20,411](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) more in lab. [$38,574](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) more in natural. [The Compression Point](#the-compression-point) explains the math
- See the [radiant cut engagement rings pillar](/radiant-cut-engagement-rings) for the full shape guide

