## The Compression Point

The Compression Point is where the lab-to-natural price ratio narrows sharply at 5ct. At 4ct, lab was 10.2× cheaper than natural. At 5ct, lab is only 4.2× cheaper — not because natural got more affordable, but because lab prices scale steeply at this weight.

The lab 5ct ring costs [$28,302](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — a [$20,411](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) jump from the [4ct lab ring at $7,891](/4-carat-radiant-cut-diamond-ring). The natural 5ct entry costs [$118,946](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — [$38,574](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) more than the [4ct natural entry at $80,372](/4-carat-radiant-cut-diamond-ring). Both costs go up, but lab's goes up steeper in percentage terms.

You still save [$90,644](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) by choosing lab at 5ct. That is a real saving. But the 10× dominance lab held at 4ct is gone — and that changes how some buyers think about this weight.

For lab buyers, the feel of the decision changes. At 4ct, you had an [$80,000](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/18152689?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) saving in front of you. At 5ct, the saving is [$90,644](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — larger in dollars, but smaller in ratio.

For natural buyers, the step is more approachable than the 4ct jump was. The 3.5ct-to-4ct wall was [$28,531](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/18152689?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) in natural. The 4ct-to-5ct jump is [$38,574](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — more in dollars, but less punishing per carat, and within reach if you were comfortable at 4ct natural pricing.

