## 5ct Radiant Cut Lab Diamond Prices

Lab 5ct radiant stones are IGI-certified and chemically identical to natural diamonds. They are not subject to any scarcity premium — which is why natural stones cost [$118,946](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and lab stones do not. All rings below use the [Ten Prong Solitaire 14K White Gold (item 311235)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at [$860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

At 5ct, the lab market has fewer options than at 4ct — just two IGI-certified stones at the same price, both D-grade at IF and FL clarity. Both cost [$27,442](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Choose based on your L:W ratio preference, not the clarity grade.

| Stone | Stone Price | Ring Total | What this means |
|-------|------------|------------|-----------------|
| [5.00ct D-IF IGI](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | [$27,442](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | [$28,302](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | **Best lab pick.** D color, IF clarity, IGI certified. Full 11mm face-up under $29,000. The [$20,411](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) jump from 4ct lab buys you 1mm more face-up and [The 11mm Statement](#the-11mm-statement). |
| [5.00ct D-FL IGI](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29314394?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | [$27,442](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29314394?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | [$28,302](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | D-FL — Flawless at the same price as D-IF. Both are correct answers at this weight. Choose the stone with the L:W ratio closest to your target — the difference between FL and IF is invisible in a radiant cut. |

**Verdict:** Both 5ct lab options arrive at [$28,302](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) complete. There is no price trade-off between D-IF and D-FL at this weight in current certified inventory — they are identically priced. The D-IF (ID: 28557750) is the recommended default. If it is unavailable, the D-FL (ID: 29314394) at the same price is equally correct.

> **Farzana on Lab 5ct:**
>
> The [$28,302](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) lab ring is not the [$7,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) lab ring from 4ct. Lab pricing scales hard at 5ct. That said, you are still saving [$90,644](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) versus the natural entry, and the stone is D-grade at IF or FL clarity on an IGI certificate.
>
> The decision at 5ct is not about lab versus natural quality. It is about what [$90,644](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) means to you. Both stones deliver 11mm of face-up radiant in the same setting — and from across the room, no one can tell the difference.

