| [5.01ct G-VVS1 GIA](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17497890?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | [$168,770](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17497890?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | [$169,630](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | G color, VVS1 clarity. [$50,684](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17497890?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) more than the G-VS1 entry for VVS1 clarity at the same color. For buyers where the VVS1 designation matters at 5ct — the F-VS1 at [$148,133](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557946?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the stronger overall value. |

