> **Farzana on Natural 5ct:**
>
> G color at VS1 clarity is not a compromise at 5ct. G reads white in white gold at this face-up size — it only shows warmth under direct side-lighting, and most people cannot see the difference from D without holding both stones next to each other. The [$118,946](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) entry gives you a GIA-certified 5ct natural radiant without overpaying for a color grade.
>
> The F-VS1 at [$148,133](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557946?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is worth the [$29,187](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557946?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) premium if you have it. F at VS1 is the best grade combination in this table. At this weight, that certificate stands on its own.

