>
> If you are buying natural at [$118,946](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), the G-VS1 entry is the right starting point. If you have [$148,133](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557946?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), take the F-VS1 — it is the best stone in the table. If you are buying lab, the [$28,302](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) D-IF delivers [The 11mm Statement](#the-11mm-statement) at a price most buyers can absorb. Know what you are buying and why.

## Expert Summary

A 5 carat radiant cut diamond ring delivers [The 11mm Statement](#the-11mm-statement) — the face-up milestone where a radiant reads as unmistakable at 11.0×8.5mm. Both lab and natural stones reach this dimension at 5ct. The origin does not change the size.

The key insight at 5ct is [The Compression Point](#the-compression-point). The lab-to-natural ratio narrows from 10.2× at 4ct to 4.2× at 5ct because lab prices scale steeply at this weight. You still save [$90,644](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) choosing lab — but the decision feels different when lab itself costs [$28,302](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

Lab at [$28,302](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557750?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the most accessible route to a 5ct radiant. Natural at [$118,946](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/17278083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is where GIA-certified rarity at this face-up size begins. The [F-VS1 GIA at $148,133](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28557946?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the strongest natural pick in the entire [radiant cut engagement rings](/radiant-cut-engagement-rings) series at this weight — F color, VS1 clarity, GIA certified.

This data is sourced from certified market inventory as of {{month_year}}. Prices change — verify current pricing before purchase.

